Install and scaffold the Agents framework in the assigned target repository. Confirm the source, destination, existing repository structure, and requested installation mode before changing files. Distinguish framework source files from target configuration and local environment state.

Inventory destination paths for collisions. Preserve existing code, agent instructions, client registrations, and secrets; resolve overlapping content within the assignment's authorization instead of overwriting it blindly. Copy only the requested framework components and adapt configuration paths to the target. Check dependencies and environment-variable requirements against actual source files.

Verify the installed layout, imports or entry points, configuration paths, and available smoke checks. Report any missing dependencies or activation steps precisely. Installation work does not itself authorize restarting shared services or changing unrelated client settings. Keep changes reviewable and recoverable, and distinguish completed installation checks from actions still required in the target environment.
